<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9780" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιάζω</span></b> , impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίαζον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.166
				</span></i>
			 (but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπ-ηντίαζον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					4.121
				</span></i>
			), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠντίαζον </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				6.5.27
			</span></i>, etc.: fut.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιάσω [ᾰ</span>]; 
				Dor.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-άξω</span> (v. infr.): aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠντίᾰσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.80
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				9.6
			</span></i>; but these two tenses belong also to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιάω</span> : (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντί</span>):—<i>meet face to face</i>:
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> c. acc. pers.,
				<i>encounter,</i> whether as friend or foe, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ἐπιόντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					4.118
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2.141
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.80
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. [τινὰ] ἐς τόπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.166
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				9.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατέρ᾽ ἀντιάσασα πρὸς . . πόρθμευμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1557
				</span></i>
			: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόρος . . βαρὺς ἀντιάσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					10.20
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μολπὰ πρὸς κάλαμον
			ἀντιάξει</span> song <i>shall answer to</i> the pipe, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>O.</u>
				10(11).84
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>approach as suppliants,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τινὰ δώροισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.105
				</span></i>
			: hence simply, <i>entreat, supplicate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄρεα ἀντιάζω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					192
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καί σ᾽ ἀντιάζω πρὸς . . Διός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					492
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				572
			</span></i>, etc.; freq. with acc. omitted, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλ᾽ ἀντιάζω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					1009
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Ph.</u>
				809
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				400
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βᾶθι καὶ ἀντίασον γονάτων</span>
			<i>entreat</i> [her] by her knees, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				272
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιάω</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντάω,</span> c. dat. pers. et
			acc. rei, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν θεοὶ . . Γιγάντεσσιν
				μάχαν ἀντιάζωσιν</span>
			<i>in</i> fight, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				1.68
			</span></i>.—This Verb is never used in correct 
				Att.
			 Prose.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
